# Paged output: PAGE= is a maximum; a page stops early when the sink has
# less than a line, a C line and the terminator of room left, but always
# sends at least one record; C means more entries exist.
> ITEM LIST PAGE=2 FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< C ITEMS1:2020202020202032:2
< .
> ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID AFTER=ITEMS1:2020202020202032:2
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 3
< .
# 680 bytes: after "+DATA", the F line and one R line (23 bytes) less
# than PROTO_ROOMMIN remain.
@ROOM 680
> ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< C ITEMS1:2020202020202031:1
< .
@ROOM 1
> ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID PAGE=25
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< C ITEMS1:2020202020202031:1
< .
@ROOM 0
> ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< R 3
< .

# Memo text written by another program: every line end dBASE knows (CR
# LF, a lone LF, a lone CR, the soft return 8D 0A), an 8D alone kept as
# it is, control bytes and 7F as \xHH, a TAB as it is.
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CPU
< +OK ID=4
@MEMO ITEMS 4 NOTES 1 a\x0Db\x0D\x0Ac\x8D\x0Ad\x0A\x0Ae\x01f\x7Fg\x09h\x0Ai\x8Dj\x0D
> ITEM NOTES 4
< +DATA
< L a
< L b
< L c
< L d
< L
< L e\x01f\x7Fg	h
< L ij
< .
# A memo whose written form passes PROTO_MAXUNPAGED is cut before the
# line that would not fit, and K TRUNCATED=1 says so.
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CPU
< +OK ID=5
@MEMO ITEMS 5 NOTES 2000 \x01
